<%# The way in, when the address has no token.

    A whole document rather than a fragment through layout: the shell expects a
    conversation behind it (a thread, a composer, an SSE stream), and none of
    that exists yet. The token is asked for once, written to the same cookie
    every page render sets, and the reader goes on to the page they asked for —
    so the URL they keep (a bookmark, the app's start url) never carries it.

    The theme is chosen before the first paint, exactly as layout does it, or a
    light-theme reader gets a flash of dark on the one screen that has no
    conversation to look at. -%>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="id">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
  <%= View.render("_appearance_head") %>
  <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark light">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#2b332f">
  <title>rubot · masuk</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/app.css?v=<%= h(asset_version) %>">
</head>
<body>
<form class="gate-card" method="post" action="/unlock">
  <h1>rubot</h1>
  <p>Alamat ini tidak membawa token. Masukkan token akses untuk melanjutkan.</p>
  <label>Token
    <input type="password" name="token" autocomplete="current-password"
           autocapitalize="off" autocorrect="off" spellcheck="false"
           required autofocus>
  </label>
  <input type="hidden" name="next" value="<%= h(next_path) %>">
  <div class="gate-row">
    <% if error %><p class="gate-error"><%= h(error) %></p><% else %><span></span><% end %>
    <button class="btn primary" type="submit">Masuk</button>
  </div>
</form>
</body>
</html>
